# Error Handling Rule

Use when writing async code, platform-specific code, or handling failures in MasterFabric.

## Pattern 1: Try-Catch with Safe Default

```dart
Future<String?> loadData() async {
  try {
    debugPrint('🔍 Loading data...');
    final result = await fetchData();
    debugPrint('✅ Data loaded successfully');
    return result;
  } catch (e) {
    debugPrint('❌ Error loading data: $e');
    return null;  // Safe default
  }
}
```

## Pattern 2: Platform-Safe Operations

```dart
Future<String?> getPlatformData() async {
  if (kIsWeb) {
    debugPrint('⚠️ Not available on web');
    return null;
  }
  try {
    return await _fetchFromNative();
  } catch (e) {
    debugPrint('❌ Error: $e');
    return null;
  }
}
```

Always check `kIsWeb` or `Platform.isX` before platform-specific code.

## Pattern 3: State-Based Error Handling (Cubits)

```dart
void loadData() async {
  stateChanger(state.copyWith(status: MyStatus.loading));
  try {
    final data = await repository.fetchData();
    stateChanger(state.copyWith(status: MyStatus.success, data: data));
  } catch (e) {
    stateChanger(state.copyWith(
      status: MyStatus.error,
      errorMessage: e.toString(),
    ));
  }
}
```

## Pattern 4: Critical Errors (FlutterError)

For unrecoverable or framework-level errors:

```dart
try {
  // critical operation
} catch (e, stack) {
  FlutterError.reportError(FlutterErrorDetails(
    exception: e,
    stack: stack,
    library: 'my_file.dart',
    context: ErrorDescription('Error doing X'),
  ));
}
```

## Emoji Logging Conventions

| Emoji | Use |
|-------|-----|
| 🚀 | Initialization, start |
| ✅ | Success |
| ❌ | Error |
| ⚠️ | Warning, fallback |
| 🔍 | Debug, loading |
| 📊 | Data, stats |

## Platform Checks

```dart
import 'package:flutter/foundation.dart' show kIsWeb;
import 'dart:io' show Platform;

if (kIsWeb) return null;
if (!Platform.isIOS && !Platform.isAndroid) return null;
```

## Checklist

- [ ] Wrap async in try-catch
- [ ] Return safe defaults (null, empty list, default value)
- [ ] Use emoji prefixes in debugPrint
- [ ] Platform check before native/platform code
- [ ] Use FlutterError.reportError for critical failures
- [ ] Avoid rethrowing unless caller should handle
